WEBVTT

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.630
2045.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.180
World War III breaks out.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.430
"Tactical Dolls Mechanical life forms
visually indistinguishable from humans."
Tactical Dolls,
indistinguishable from humans,

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.270
"Tactical Dolls Mechanical life forms
visually indistinguishable from humans."
are deployed by military
organizations all around the world.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.570
And after the war ends,

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.950
the T-Dolls of the major military
manufacturer, Sangvis Ferri,

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.620
"Sangvis Ferri A major military
manufacturing company that
rebelled against humanity."
suddenly rebel against humanity.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.370
"Sangvis Ferri A major military
manufacturing company that
rebelled against humanity."
The private military company, Griffin,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.830
"Griffin A private military company."
The private military company, Griffin,

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:40.950
"Griffin A private military company."
sends its elite AR Team to find the cause
of the rebellion and put a stop to it.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.870
"AR Team Griffin's elite T-Doll unit."
sends its elite AR Team to find the cause
of the rebellion and put a stop to it.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.710
sends its elite AR Team to find the cause
of the rebellion and put a stop to it.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.580
Sangvis reinforcements incoming!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.000
Estimated arrival time, 15 seconds!

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.500
There are too many!

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.550
Try to save ammo!

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.930
It's all they can do to
take care of themselves!

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.590
They don't have the strength to...

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.470
I've come to deliver death.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.280
Hello, Commander!

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:19.160
I'm Griffin's forward command
post logistics officer, Kalina!

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.950
My name is Gentiane.
I was just assigned here today.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.580
You must be tired from your long journey.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.540
Were there any problems?

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:36.300
I don't know if it's a problem, but...
It wasn't what I'd call comfortable.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.930
Oh, things can be a little
violent around here.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.640
The vehicles all get
banged up in combat real fast.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.140
I didn't get any sleep because of it.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.020
I know I just got here,
but I'm going to take a nap.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.690
Did you receive a rundown on your mission?

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.150
A basic one.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:58.570
Use Griffin dolls to put down the
out-of-control Sangvis, right?

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.570
There's a little more to it than that.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:03.240
Please use this room.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:08.500
Heaven...

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.920
Hey, what's next on my schedule?

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.670
Your first mission's in an hour.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.520
A mission an hour after I get here?

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.770
I might've picked the
wrong place to get hired.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:58.440
Sorry... Sangvis has been
more aggressive lately.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:00.070
Got any info on the enemy?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.280
Yes.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.700
They're not dolls?

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.790
They use these as scouts
a lot of the time.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.250
Um, do you have any
actual combat experience?

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.210
Only in the simulator.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.090
Today's my first real fight.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.470
Show me the data on the dolls.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.470
Okay.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:28.260
There's another operation
running parallel to yours.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:33.180
Some of the dolls are recovering.
Can you pick your team from this list?

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.230
Can I talk to them?

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.400
Talk to them?

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.790
MP5? I'm Gentiane.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.420
A new commander who just arrived today.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.130
H-Hello, Commander!

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:03.010
I want to ask you something
before the mission.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.010
Is that all right?

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.590
A-Ask anything, please!

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.720
Okay, thanks.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.350
You're a sniper out on a mission.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:14.850
But there's a problem with your gun,

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.940
and there's a chance it
will explode when fired.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.770
It's a 50/50 chance.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.980
Your only other weapon is a handgun.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:26.530
But you're confident you can hit
your target with the sniper rifle.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.780
Which will you chose?

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.410
Neither!

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.290
I'd abandon the mission!

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.710
Why?

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:40.840
If elements of the mission are uncertain,
it's better to try again another day.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.170
Otherwise, I wouldn't be
able to concentrate on it.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:47.010
Okay. Got it.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.180
How many dummies can you make?

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.720
Three, four...

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.930
Four!

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.720
No more questions.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.600
Thank you.

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.480
B-Bye!

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.900
Did you learn anything from that?

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.780
She's a bit of a child in some ways,

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.990
but much more grown-up than she looks.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.740
Having a girl like her along will mean
fewer mistakes and oversights.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.830
But what I really wanted to know

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:18.790
was if she could make a decision
beyond the ones I'd offered her.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.710
The battlefield is constantly changing
into an infinity of possible patterns.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:26.210
I wanted to know what she would do
when confronted with the unexpected.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.840
I can use her.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.350
I'm so nervous.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:37.810
Hello there.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:40.440
I-I'm FN49!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.520
N-Nice to meet you!

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.160
Submachine guns to the front.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.320
One Assault Rifle to the rear.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:54.990
That'll improve accuracy.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.330
Got it!

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:58.540
Let's get ready!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.310
Everybody, can you hear me?

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:21.190
Our objective is to remove enemies
along the route. Eliminate them.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:30.450
There are two types of enemies known to
be in the area, Prowlers and Dinergates.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.740
The operation doesn't end
until you're all home safe.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.030
Make sure not to get hurt.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.130
Begin the mission.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.290
MP5, go to the front.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.080
The rest, provide support from the rear.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.580
Okay!

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.080
As you wish.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.580
Like this?

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.250
I'm hungry!

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:29.840
You just ate, FNC!

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.590
And you guys are dolls, right?

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.550
Why do you get hungry?

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:38.100
That's just how we're made.
Don't blame me!

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.820
Commander, I've sighted the enemy.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.150
Displaying on monitor!

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.360
They haven't found us yet!

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.650
Lucky us!

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:56.740
It's not luck.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.080
On uneven ground, you guys can
get to better positions more easily

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:05.000
than robots on wheels or with four legs.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:08.340
That's why you dropped us
somewhere far away?

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.300
I had you run to get there, though.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.090
The lead is in range.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:14.510
Shall I destroy it?

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:15.340
Wait.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.840
Withdraw behind cover.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.260
Roger.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:22.970
MP5, lay down automatic
gun fire from the front.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:24.770
Delay the unit.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.020
Okay!

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.900
FNC, G36, help her.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.270
Understood.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.610
Okay!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:35.200
P7, get up high and aim
for the enemy cameras.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.320
I'm the only one who has the hard job!

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.030
No complaining.

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:43.700
You've got an S in accuracy,
so I'm counting on you.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:46.120
Commander, we're in position!

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.500
Stay there until further orders.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.250
Roger.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.880
You're not opening fire?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:56.420
If we draw them a little closer,
we can hit them all with a single attack.

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.720
If we fired now, the enemies at the
front would shield those in the back,

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.220
and they'd be unharmed.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:08.060
Open fire!

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.250
Cease fire!

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:33.000
MP5, give me a sitrep.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:44.010
All enemy units down!

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:45.680
Damage on our side is...

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:51.100
This is P7! No moderate or total damage!

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.020
None!

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:56.230
No moderate or total damage!

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.740
We're all fully operational!

00:10:58.740 --> 00:10:59.990
Okay.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:03.120
Get to the point and wait
for the recovery helicopter.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.370
Okay!

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.080
Mission complete.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.330
Good work.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:15.250
Well, I'm glad nobody was injured.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:17.550
Um...

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:20.050
I didn't explain earlier,

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:24.600
but all the dolls have backups of
their memories and experiences.

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.930
Even if they're totally destroyed,
they can be recovered.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:28.930
I know.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:31.980
Doesn't it kind of upset you
to see dolls get destroyed?

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:34.980
What's next?

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:39.490
In six hours, you have
a meeting with Helian.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:43.030
I'll sleep until then.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:59.010
Your first mission went well, it seems.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.840
Well, it was the tutorial.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:05.140
You noticed, then.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:09.850
Low-priority objectives.
Enemies with simple attack patterns.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:13.100
Geography with easily-determined
advantageous points.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.440
In other words,

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:19.610
it was a test for a commander with
no combat experience, wasn't it?

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.700
Don't get so upset.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:24.610
It's been eleven years
since the end of the war,

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.490
and one year since Sangvis's
Elisa went out of control.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.870
Both enemies and allies are dolls.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:34.370
The war going on here is like none
humanity has ever seen before.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:37.790
The rules are different from what we knew,

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:42.340
which means we need a
special type of commander.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:46.590
And we won't find them just
by looking in the military.

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:49.720
We recruit directly from
the military schools.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:52.310
That's the kind of recruiting
only a private company can do.

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.350
Well, thank you.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:57.060
What we needed to know
immediately was this:

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:03.820
How do you pick your autonomous dolls?
How do you control them? How do you fight?

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.950
In other words, how capable
you'd be in an actual battle.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.490
And what did you find?

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:14.750
You're a little too emotionally
attached to the dolls, but...

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.500
...you're usable.

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.040
You pass.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:23.260
Welcome to Griffin, Gentiane.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.600
Commander!

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:39.520
Master! No--Commander...

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:43.990
Thanks to your orders, we were
able to keep damage to a minimum!

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.150
Nice work!

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:48.070
Thank you so much!

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:49.660
Sorry...

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.990
They all wanted to say thanks to you.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:55.000
To me?

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.250
Have some chocolate.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:58.500
T-Thanks...

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:02.550
Please... use me next time!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:03.760
Me too!

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.590
I can't wait to get some exercise!

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:10.260
Everyone, you're bothering the commander.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:12.350
All of you do it at once.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.020
Ready...

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:17.850
Welcome to Griffin, Commander Gentiane!

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:21.900
Nice to meet you all.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.630
Ingram!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.930
I refuse to accept it...
I refuse to accept it!

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:54.140
What's wrong?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:56.060
The commander...

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.020
Attention, all commanders.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:06.860
This information was recovered
on the front lines today by Ingram.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:12.410
Her combat team encountered a
Sangvis unit during operational action.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:16.910
A High-End Model Scarecrow
was commanding the enemy.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:21.540
It almost completely
annihilated Ingram's unit.

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:26.630
Ingram left the battlefield to bring back
this information and the combat data.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:32.510
She succeeded in escaping, but one
of her unit's Skorpions was imprisoned.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:35.720
From several of the conversation
patterns exchanged during the battle,

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:38.770
we can assume that
Scarecrow knows the reason

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:42.690
for the Sangvis attacks in the area.

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:46.400
Thus, we are executing
an emergency operation.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:50.150
The goal is to make contact
with and destroy Scarecrow,

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:53.410
and recover her memory module.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:57.040
At the same time, we will
rescue and recover Skorpion.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.540
Data will be sent soon
to participating units.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.330
Dismissed.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.960
What's a High-End Model?

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:09.420
Sangvis T-Dolls with exceptionally
strong combat skills.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.890
They use special equipment,
so it's hard to take them down.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.290
Cease fire!

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.420
Confirmed hit!

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:49.050
Remaining enemies: zero!

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.470
The enemy area is now under our control!

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:03.640
Are you sure about that?

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.270
When did she get here?

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:09.940
I didn't hear any footsteps!

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:12.110
Hello.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:16.200
And please die.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:18.700
You're Scarecrow, aren't you?

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:20.200
Yes.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:22.540
We will now capture you.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.370
Surrender quietly.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:28.840
Me? Surrender to Griffin's scrap dolls?

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:31.170
That's not funny.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:34.220
This area is under our control.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:35.930
There's nowhere to run.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:41.510
We have things to ask you--
no, your module.

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:42.810
Surrender.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:44.890
We'll give you three seconds.

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.440
Three...

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:50.440
Two...

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:51.320
One...

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.780
Initiating annihilation mission.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:17:59.990
Con fuoco!

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.620
Open fire!

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.790
Animato!

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:18.050
You have no chance of winning.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:20.180
So this is a High-End Model...

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:25.180
Are you ready?

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:27.730
Scarecrow is about to go on the move.

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.900
Carry out the mission as planned.

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.060
Roger.

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:34.530
Pathetic.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.030
Griffin's dolls are as weak as I thought.

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.700
Open fire!

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:57.800
A pincer attack?

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:01.590
It was a clever idea, using your
primary force as a diversion.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:06.600
But did you really think you could
beat me with such limited firepower?

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.440
Not in the least.

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:10.600
But it's not just "us."

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.700
I'll pay you back 100 times
for what you did to me!

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:22.370
Everyone! Full-auto fire!

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:44.180
There's no way for you to fight back now.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:49.060
I can't believe it's ending like this.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:50.310
Give it up.

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.350
We rescued Skorpion.

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:55.730
Any information she gave you was fake.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.570
Fake?

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:03.780
We know how your dolls' AIs work.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:07.410
When those inferior dolls lie,

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:14.290
they mix random false data with the truth,
swapping the order it appears in.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:20.420
Thus, if we get even three false
statements from her and analyze them,

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:23.510
we can find the commonalities.

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:26.810
That is, the real information.

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:30.850
That information on the
AI program is highly classified!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:32.690
How did you know it?

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:37.730
Who are you?

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:44.740
Just a low-ranking doll sent from Sangvis.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:51.200
But still, I'm different than a tool
that just follows human orders.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:54.170
You wouldn't understand.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:21:00.090
You humans who hide in your bases,
and only show yourselves via video.

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:02.920
Talk all you like.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:07.260
No matter what you know, you won't
be able to share it with your comrades.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:11.930
Actually, I'm sharing with them right now.

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:21.280
Process number 8354 9266 0233...

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:25.070
I was able to calculate it
just before the very end...

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:28.780
M4A1's coordinates.

00:21:29.870 --> 00:21:32.000
I heard you, Scarecrow.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.410
Well done.

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:37.380
Thanks. It's up to you now.

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:41.590
Now, goodbye.

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:43.130
She's going to self-destruct!

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:45.090
Get out of there now, everyone!

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:49.010
Oh? The commander from before?

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:51.560
You're quite emotional.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:55.190
Are you new, then?

00:21:55.190 --> 00:22:00.320
Welcome to the frontline, <i>fräulein</i>.

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:14.160
MP5...

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:17.580
P7...

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:19.330
G36...

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:21.960
FNC...

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:26.720
Any surviving units, confirm the
situation and recover the module.

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:38.350
If I'd known, I would've
given you more attention.

00:22:39.770 --> 00:22:44.070
Now leave it to me and rest, Scarecrow.

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:49.160
I'll find you... M4A1.

00:24:43.020 --> 00:24:45.730
Episode 3: "The Echo."
